Description: Analysis pipeline for a retrospective cohort of 4,635 first
    conventional IVF cycles, developing and internally validating a
    ten-predictor random forest model for low fertilization rate or total
    fertilization failure, defined as a two-pronuclear fertilization rate
    below 30 percent. Covers data preparation, multiple imputation,
    collinearity diagnostics, two-stage model selection across nine
    algorithms, internal validation, SHAP-based interpretation and generation
    of all manuscript figures and tables.
